Note: TestFastEqTrivialEncodingAndDecoding exercises 12 alphabets x 255 lengths x
100 iterations, comparing the fast and trivial paths and their round-trips -- all
routed through the Rust implementation. The two tests that require Go package
internals (hardening_test.go's TestMulAddBase58WordsLEMatchesBigInt, and the
leading-zero test that reads the unexported Alphabet.encode field) are covered by
the translated Rust suite (tests/parity.rs) and the fast.rs unit test instead.
